urge before relight"},{"node":"HT shift converter","deviation":"High temperature","cause":"Low steam, high CO in feed","consequence":"Catalyst sintering, vessel overheating","safeguard":"Bed thermocouples and high temperature trip"},{"node":"PSA unit","deviation":"Valve fails open","cause":"Valve or controller failure","consequence":"Impure hydrogen to users, overpressure of tail gas system","safeguard":"Online H2 purity analyser, relief on tail gas drum, valve position monitoring"},{"node":"Hydrogen product line","deviation":"Loss of containment","cause":"Flange leak, hydrogen attack","consequence":"Jet fire or vapour cloud explosion","safeguard":"Gas detection, Nelson curve material selection, emergency shutdown and depressurising"}],"process_hazards":[{"hazard":"Pressure","detail":"Up to 32 bar. Relief valves sized for fire and blocked outlet."},{"hazard":"High temperature","detail":"Up to 870 C. Creep, hydrogen attack and burns; refractory and tube skin temperature monitoring."},{"hazard":"Flammable materials","detail":"Carbon monoxide, Methane, Hydrogen. Hazardous area classification, ignition source control, gas detection, fire protection."},{"hazard":"Toxic materials","detail":"Carbon monoxide. Toxic gas detection, emergency shutdown and isolation, escape sets, minimise inventory."}],"validation":[{"metric":"Natural gas, feed + fuel, per Nm3 H2","model":15.114863,"published":14.212,"unit":"MJ(LHV)/Nm3 H2","error_pct":6.35282,"inside_range":null,"source":"IEAGHG Technical Report 2017/02, base case without CCS, Table 2","url":"https://ieaghg.org/publications/2017-02%20Techno%20-%20Economic%20Evaluation%20of%20SMR%20Based%20Standalone%20(Merchant)%20Hydrogen%20Plant%20with%20CCS.pdf","note":"","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":10,"pass":true},{"metric":"Direct CO2 per Nm3 H2","model":0.830212,"published":0.8091,"unit":"kg CO2/Nm3 H2","error_pct":2.60931,"inside_range":null,"source":"IEAGHG Technical Report 2017/02, base case without CCS","url":"https://ieaghg.org/publications/2017-02%20Techno%20-%20Economic%20Evaluation%20of%20SMR%20Based%20Standalone%20(Merchant)%20Hydrogen%20Plant%20with%20CCS.pdf","note":"","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":10,"pass":true},{"metric":"Stack CO2 per kg H2","model":9.230892,"published":9.3,"unit":"kg CO2/kg H2","error_pct":-0.743099,"inside_range":null,"source":"NETL 2022, Comparison of fossil hydrogen technologies, Case 1 SMR without capture","url":"https://netl.doe.gov/projects/files/ComparisonofCommercialStateofArtFossilBasedHydrogenProductionTechnologies_041222.pdf","note":"","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":15,"pass":true},{"metric":"Methane conversion in the reformer","model":78.210807,"published":77,"unit":"%","error_pct":1.572477,"inside_range":null,"source":"NETL 2022, Case 1: S/C 2.56, 870 C, 2.8 MPa, 'more than 77 percent'","url":"https://netl.doe.gov/projects/files/ComparisonofCommercialStateofArtFossilBasedHydrogenProductionTechnologies_041222.pdf","note":"Published figure is a lower bound at nearly the same conditions as the default.","kind":"thermo","tolerance_pct":10,"pass":true},{"metric":"Export steam energy","model":16.374572,"published":26,"unit":"MJ/kg H2","error_pct":-37.020875,"inside_range":null,"source":"NETL 2022, Case 1 modelled steam output 514 GJ/h","url":"https://netl.doe.gov/projects/files/ComparisonofCommercialStateofArtFossilBasedHydrogenProductionTechnologies_041222.pdf","note":"NETL exports superheated steam from a plant about 4.8 times this size; steam conditions differ.","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":50,"pass":true},{"metric":"Fixed capital vs published range","model":49917714.709225,"published":[92081586.756211,165746856.16118],"unit":"USD (2024)","error_pct":-45.789689,"inside_range":false,"source":"IEA, The Future of Hydrogen (2019): SMR without CCUS USD 500 to 900 per kW H2 (2018). Escalated with CEPCI 603.1 (2018) to 800.0","url":"https://iea.blob.core.windows.net/assets/9e3a3493-b9a6-4b7d-b499-7ca48e357561/The_Future_of_Hydrogen.pdf","note":"Factored Turton estimate; the PSA is costed as adsorber vessels only, not as a vendor package.","kind":"capex","tolerance_pct":50,"pass":true}],"assumptions":["Natural gas is modelled as pure methane, already desulphurised. Gas is available at reformer pressure.","Reformer and HT shift reach ideal gas chemical equilibrium. Defaults follow NETL 2022 Case 1 (S/C 2.56, 870 C, 2.8 MPa), rounded.","PSA recovers 89% of the hydrogen fed (IEAGHG 2017/02 quotes 85 to 90%) as pure product; all other species and the remaining hydrogen leave in the tail gas.","Furnace: tail gas plus trim gas with 10% excess air (combustion air preheated to 250 C against flue gas at the cold end). Flue gas leaves the radiant box at 1000 C and the stack at 160 C; trim gas is solved so the radiant heat equals the reformer duty. No casing losses. Fans 50 mbar, 70%.","Convection section preheats the mixed feed to 620 C and raises 40 bar steam with the rest. Heat from the reformed gas down to the shift inlet and 85% of the shift effluent heat above 150 C also raise steam. Steam left after the process steam is exported.","PSA adsorber vessels sized at a gas hourly space velocity of 1,000 per hour (ten beds as one item).","No CO2 capture: all feed and fuel carbon leaves in the reformer flue gas."],"notes":[]}